Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:13:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] exl3 cuda: the common prompt kernels take 3-bit mcg
 gate/up and down, by projection group

tf_exl3_prompt_gu_k6 and tf_exl3_prompt_down_k6 run the transposed prompt
kernels on 96-byte (3-bit) mcg tiles, with tf_exl3_prompt_gu/_down's
arguments. The kernels are templated on the half-bit width; the 4-bit
entry points keep their SASS byte for byte on sm_80/86/89/120/121 (nvcc
13.3). The down kernel reads its item in the kernel itself so that its
launch bound still limits the thread arithmetic.

Layer gains uniform_k2_gu and uniform_k2_d (the loader's per-group
verified widths, uniform_k2 when zero). The prompt path takes a layer
whose gate/up width and down width are each 6 or 8 and launches each
group's own kernel; widths that disagree with uniform_k2 stay unverified
and keep the grouped path. Scratch is width-independent.

Contract: both launches registered pending nvcc 13.0's receipts, with
nvcc 13.3's five-SM usage measured by kernel-contract-limits.

